cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TRACE, please cite it as below."
title: "TRACE: Transparent Recording of AI-assisted Collaboration Experiments"
abstract: >-
  TRACE is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that produces a standardized,
  human-readable audit trail for AI-assisted research and software workflows. It
  records decision-level provenance: who proposed each step, who accepted, revised,
  or rejected it, the rationale, and how the approach evolved, and exports to W3C
  PROV as JSON-LD.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Oliver
    family-names: Muellerklein
    email: omuellerklein@berkeley.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Environmental Science, Policy, and Management, University of California, Berkeley"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5967-1314"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Thru-Echoes/TRACE"
version: 0.5.1
date-released: 2026-09-04
# The concept DOI resolves to the most recent archived version, so a citation
# made with it stays valid across releases. Version-specific DOIs are listed
# under identifiers for anyone pinning to one exact archive; a release's own
# version DOI is added here once the archive that mints it exists, so this file
# never names a DOI that does not resolve.
